# 必考词 Unit11
# 领域: 考研
# 学科: 英语词汇
# 来源: 2023红宝书考研英语词汇-必考词
# 描述: 必考词Unit11核心高频词汇

{{foundation}}{/faʊnˈdeɪʃn/}}{n. 基础；基金会}}{{Education is the foundation of personal development.}}

{{fraction}}{/ˈfrækʃn/}}{n. 分数；小部分；片段}}{{Only a fraction of the applicants were accepted.}}

{{framework}}{/ˈfreɪmwɜːrk/}}{n. 框架；结构}}{{The report provides a framework for future research.}}

{{frequent}}{/ˈfriːkwənt/}}{adj. 频繁的；经常的}}{{Frequent exercise is beneficial to health.}}

{{friction}}{/ˈfrɪkʃn/}}{n. 摩擦；不和}}{{There is always some friction between the two departments.}}

{{frontier}}{/frʌnˈtɪər/}}{n. 边界；前沿}}{{Space is often called the final frontier.}}

{{frustrate}}{/frʌˈstreɪt/}}{v. 使沮丧；挫败}}{{The lack of progress frustrated the entire team.}}

{{fulfil/fulfill}}{/fʊlˈfɪl/}}{v. 实现；履行}}{{She fulfilled her dream of becoming a doctor.}}

{{function}}{/ˈfʌŋkʃn/}}{n. 功能；职责；v. 运作}}{{The main function of the heart is to pump blood.}}

{{fund}}{/fʌnd/}}{n. 基金；资金；v. 资助}}{{The research was funded by the government.}}

{{fundamental}}{/ˌfʌndəˈmentl/}}{adj. 基本的；根本的}}{{Freedom of speech is a fundamental human right.}}

{{generate}}{/ˈdʒenəreɪt/}}{v. 产生；引起}}{{Solar panels generate electricity from sunlight.}}

{{generation}}{/ˌdʒenəˈreɪʃn/}}{n. 一代人；产生}}{{The younger generation is more open to new ideas.}}

{{generous}}{/ˈdʒenərəs/}}{adj. 慷慨的；大方的}}{{She is generous with her time and money.}}

{{genius}}{/ˈdʒiːniəs/}}{n. 天才；天赋}}{{Einstein was a genius who revolutionized physics.}}

{{genuine}}{/ˈdʒenjuɪn/}}{adj. 真正的；真诚的}}{{She showed genuine concern for her friend's well-being.}}

{{gesture}}{/ˈdʒestʃər/}}{n. 姿态；手势}}{{Offering help was a kind gesture that everyone appreciated.}}

{{global}}{/ˈɡləʊbl/}}{adj. 全球的；全面的}}{{Global warming is a serious threat to the planet.}}

{{govern}}{/ˈɡʌvrn/}}{v. 统治；管理}}{{The country is governed by a democratic system.}}

{{grab}}{/ɡræb/}}{v. 抓取；夺取}}{{He grabbed his bag and rushed out the door.}}

{{grace}}{/ɡreɪs/}}{n. 优雅；恩惠}}{{She moved with grace and confidence on stage.}}

{{gradual}}{/ˈɡrædʒuəl/}}{adj. 逐渐的；渐进的}}{{There has been a gradual improvement in the economy.}}

{{grant}}{/ɡrɑːnt/}}{v. 授予；n. 补助金}}{{The university granted him a scholarship for his excellent performance.}}

{{grasp}}{/ɡrɑːsp/}}{v./n. 抓住；理解}}{{He quickly grasped the main idea of the article.}}

{{gratitude}}{/ˈɡrætɪtjuːd/}}{n. 感激；感谢}}{{She expressed her gratitude for the generous donation.}}

{{gravity}}{/ˈɡrævəti/}}{n. 重力；严重性}}{{The gravity of the situation demanded immediate attention.}}

{{grief}}{/ɡriːf/}}{n. 悲伤；忧伤}}{{She was overcome with grief after the loss of her mother.}}

{{gross}}{/ɡrəʊs/}}{adj. 总的；严重的}}{{The gross domestic product increased by 5% last year.}}

{{guarantee}}{/ˌɡærənˈtiː/}}{v./n. 保证；担保}}{{The product comes with a two-year guarantee.}}

{{guard}}{/ɡɑːrd/}}{v./n. 守卫；保护}}{{The guards stood at the entrance of the building.}}

{{guide}}{/ɡaɪd/}}{v. 指导；n. 指南}}{{The professor guided the students through the research process.}}

{{guilty}}{/ˈɡɪlti/}}{adj. 有罪的；内疚的}}{{The jury found the defendant guilty of fraud.}}

{{halt}}{/hɔːlt/}}{v./n. 停止；中断}}{{Production was halted due to a shortage of materials.}}

{{handle}}{/ˈhændl/}}{v. 处理；n. 把手}}{{She handles pressure very well under tight deadlines.}}

{{harmony}}{/ˈhɑːrməni/}}{n. 和谐；融洽}}{{The community lives in harmony with nature.}}

{{harsh}}{/hɑːrʃ/}}{adj. 严厉的；恶劣的}}{{The harsh winter made travel extremely difficult.}}

{{harvest}}{/ˈhɑːrvɪst/}}{n./v. 收获；收割}}{{The farmers celebrated a bountiful harvest this year.}}

{{hesitate}}{/ˈhezɪteɪt/}}{v. 犹豫；踌躇}}{{Do not hesitate to ask if you need any help.}}

{{highlight}}{/ˈhaɪlaɪt/}}{v. 强调；n. 亮点}}{{The report highlights the need for environmental protection.}}

{{horizon}}{/həˈraɪzn/}}{n. 地平线；视野}}{{The sun slowly sank below the horizon.}}
